  I finally have gotten what I consider to be a final (or nearly final)
version of Nethack 3.0 on the PC.  It has all the options I mentioned in
the previous message as well as KOPS and PROBING.  The final executable
size is 574K.  I accomplished this by changing the optimization used by
Microsoft C to -Oasn instead of -Oat which was in the Makefile.  To run it,
you need a REALLY bare bones system.  Running DOS 3.3, I had to take out
all my environment variables except for TERM and TERMCAP, and set BUFFERS
and FILES to 5.  Anything more will cause errors about not enough environment
space.  You need 600K+ free memory to run the game.  Also, my compiled
version is for computers which can handle the 80186 instruction set, namely,
the V-20, 80186, 80286, 80386, and up (80486 anyone?).  

  I am making the file available for anonymous FTP from my Sun station here.
It is rather slow, so I would prefer that people get it at late-night times
when I am not using it.  The system is lampwick.berkeley.edu (128.32.131.141).
In fact, if someone could stick this file on some other system, it would
be great.   There are two files, NH30EXE.ZIP and NH30SUP.ZIP - one contains
the executable file only, the other contains all the supplementary stuff
you need.  

  Anyway, have fun playing Nethack 3.0 - it seems to be stable and I haven't
seen it crash at all.

  If anyone comes up with a version which has all the options using overlays
or something - please let me know!


